 "reference_key": "liang2009multi",
 "comment": "Liang et al. 2009 (MBEC 47:743) Fig. 4: the normal ascending-aortic pressure (b), fitted, and the normal LV pressure (a) and P-V loop volumes (e), held out. Set-up (validation.lv.harness): a minimal LV loop, left-atrial pressure source -> mitral valve -> this chamber (lv) driven by cardiac_clock Liang2009_v01 -> aortic valve -> aortic root (arterial_simple vv) -> systemic terminal (terminal pp_spec_I) -> venous outlet pressure. Liang's own model has a 55-artery 1-D tree; the loop stands in for it with an afterload (aortic root and systemic terminal R and C) calibrated to Liang's aortic pressure, so the LV pressure curve (Fig. 4a) is then the held-out check of the chamber. The LV dead volume q_us is fitted too, with the P-V loop features (end-diastolic and end-systolic volumes, Fig. 4e): Liang states no dead volume, and with his E_B and end-diastolic pressure his EDV implies ~26 ml, not Korakianitis's 5 ml (review 2026-10-12). std 2 mmHg (digitising). To redo: pytest tests/test_modules.py --component chamber/vv -k \"calibrate and lv\" --include-unreviewed",
